tip: | Look at the engine. | Long things are mostly the same part again and again. Draw one wheel well and copy it along the axis.
tip: 1 | Three masses. | Frame, boiler and cab. The boiler is a half cylinder pushed along the grid, the same trick as the mailbox.
tip: 3 | Bands along the tube. | Along a cylinder the light runs in long stripes, as on the barrel but lying down. Brass rings break it into even lengths.
tip: 4 | Repeat, then break the rhythm. | Three big wheels and two small ones, and one rod joining them. A pattern with an exception looks designed.
